From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shawn-makes-stuff <shawn.rains@rocketmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:06:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] firmware: COSMOS MCU patches in Rust (drv8833, hx711s,
 stm32 RS-485 DE pin)

- src/drv8833.rs: COSMOS 0003 drv8833.c (hall speed PID / manual duty)
- src/sensor_hx711s.rs: COSMOS 0007 sensor_hx711s.c (multi-chip HX711)
- stm32/serial.rs: COSMOS 0005 RS-485 driver enable pin + turnaround
- configs cosmos-{cc1,cc2}-{bed,toolhead,canvas}, cosmos-afc-lite-usb from
  COSMOS's board configs; C references from the COSMOS tree
  (rusticc/tools/mkref_cosmos.sh) equal the CC1's shipped dictionaries
- ctr_check 7/7 identical; emu_cmp 8/8 on cc1-bed, cc2-canvas (RS-485
  DE / TCIE accesses identical), afc-lite-usb (tests/cosmos/cosmos.script)
- emu_run.py: usart on alternate pins, TCIE

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
